From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:54:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 49/49] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475: describe UFS operating points
 with CX levels

The SM8475 UFS host used the legacy freq-table-hz property, which scales
the core and UniPro clocks without any RPMh CX performance vote. Once
fw_devlink sync_state() releases the boot-time votes, CX can sit at
LOW_SVS while the UFS clocks run at a rate that needs a higher corner.

Switch to an OPP table, following upstream commit 2f7be4caacd2
("arm64: dts: qcom: sm8550: Switch UFS from opp-table-hz to opp-v2"),
including the node-level NOM vote. Like Qualcomm's downstream cape
device tree (freq-table 75/850 MHz with multi-level clock scaling),
describe two operating points: 75 MHz at LOW_SVS, which ufs-qcom maps
to HS-G1, and 850 MHz at TURBO_L1, mapped to HS-G4. The downstream GCC
driver allows 850 MHz on gcc_ufs_phy_axi_clk_src, the UniPro core and
the ICE core clock sources only at its VDD_HIGH_L1 level.

The 850 MHz rate needs the controller's turbo configuration, so use
the "qcom,sm8475-ufshc" compatible, with the SM8450 fallback. With
these two points the link never runs HS-G4 without it. Downstream also
drops from 850 MHz to 300 MHz/NOM at HS-G4 while the controller is less
than half busy; that level is not described.

No equivalent SM8450 or SM8475 patch was found upstream or on the lists.

Reference: LineageOS/android_kernel_qcom_sm8450 lineage-20
952aa00564cbb2cc788378c97e08958c4b889758, drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-waipio.c
(gcc_cape_fixup(), rate_max per VDD level) and the Lenovo TB320FC stock
device tree (ufshc@1d84000).

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
index 47c20b6997e0..eeb93f0628ca 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
@@ -73,15 +73,41 @@ &tlmm {
 };
 
 &ufs_mem_hc {
-	freq-table-hz =
-		<75000000 300000000>,
-		<0 0>,
-		<0 0>,
-		<75000000 300000000>,
-		<0 0>,
-		<0 0>,
-		<0 0>,
-		<0 0>;
+	compatible = "qcom,sm8475-ufshc", "qcom,sm8450-ufshc", "qcom,ufshc",
+		     "jedec,ufs-2.0";
+
+	/delete-property/ freq-table-hz;
+
+	required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_nom>;
+	operating-points-v2 = <&ufs_opp_table>;
+
+	ufs_opp_table: opp-table {
+		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+
+		opp-75000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <75000000>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <0>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <0>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <75000000>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <0>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <0>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <0>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <0>;
+			required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
+		};
+
+		opp-850000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <850000000>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <0>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <0>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <850000000>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <0>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <0>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <0>,
+				 /bits/ 64 <0>;
+			required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_turbo_l1>;
+		};
+	};
 };
 
 &videocc {
